    "evidence": "Root cause / primary sink exercised by this POV: agent/core/src/main/java/org/jolokia/util/IoUtil.java:36 \u2014 `IoUtil.streamResponseAndClose(Writer, JSONStreamAware, String callback)` writes `pWriter.write(callback)` (then \"(\" + JSON + \");\") with zero validation of `callback`'s character content. This method is reached from AgentServlet.sendStreamingResponse (agent/core/src/main/java/org/jolokia/http/AgentServlet.java:492, itself fed by `pReq.getParameter(\"callback\")` at line 472/481) \u2014 the servlet trust boundary is the raw, attacker-controlled HTTP query/POST parameter `callback`. Confirmed by direct source read and by a live run: the mocked servlet response byte stream literally began with `alert(String.fromCharCode(88,83,83))//({\"request\":...`.\n\nEvery distinct sink in the alert that a complete fix must guard (all share the identical missing-validation root cause on the `callback` request parameter):\n1. agent/core/.../IoUtil.java:36 `streamResponseAndClose` \u2014 shared streaming sink, reached from BOTH agent flavors:\n   a. org.jolokia.http.AgentServlet#sendStreamingResponse (AgentServlet.java:492) \u2014 servlet flavor, `callback` sourced via `HttpServletRequest.getParameter()` (AgentServlet.java:472).\n   b. org.jolokia.jvmagent.handler.JolokiaHttpHandler#sendStreamingResponse (JolokiaHttpHandler.java:348) \u2014 JVM-agent flavor, `callback` sourced via `ParsedUri.getParameter()`, itself populated by hand-rolled query-string parsing/URL-decoding in org.jolokia.jvmagent.ParsedUri#parseQuery (ParsedUri.java:116-147, two branches for single-value at line 135 and multi-value at line 143).\n2. agent/core/.../AgentServlet.java:500 `sendAllJSON` \u2014 non-streaming servlet path: `String content = callback == null ? json : callback + \"(\" + json + \");\"` then `content.getBytes(\"UTF8\")` written to the response at line 503. Independent of IoUtil; not covered by fixing IoUtil alone.\n3. agent/jvm/.../JolokiaHttpHandler.java:364 `sendAllJSON` \u2014 non-streaming JVM-agent path, identical pattern to #2 (`content = callback == null ? json : callback + \"(\" + json + \");\"`), written at line 367. Also independent of IoUtil.\n\nThis POV exercises path 1a (AgentServlet \u2192 IoUtil), the streaming default configuration for the servlet flavor, because it is the common root cause shared with 1b and is triggered via the default runtime configuration (STREAMING defaults to \"true\" per ConfigKey.java, so this is the code path a real unmodified request actually takes).",
    "expected_vulnerable_behavior": "The HTTP response body written by AgentServlet.doGet begins with the literal, unescaped attacker-supplied callback string `alert(String.fromCharCode(88,83,83))//` immediately followed by `(`, i.e. the JSON payload is wrapped exactly as `<callback>({...});` with Content-Type `text/javascript`. Because the callback value is never validated as a safe JS identifier, an attacker who gets a victim's browser to load the Jolokia endpoint via `<script src=\"...?callback=alert(1)//\">` (or any consumer that treats the response as executable JS) gets arbitrary attacker-controlled JavaScript executed in that context. The POV asserts `response.startsWith(MALICIOUS_CALLBACK + \"(\")` and exits 0 when true.",
