    "regression_hint": "Invariant a correct fix must enforce, applied uniformly at (or before) every sink listed above: the `callback` value must be validated as a syntactically-safe JavaScript identifier/reference expression (e.g. matching something like `^[a-zA-Z0-9_$]+(\\.[a-zA-Z0-9_$]+|\\[[0-9]+\\])*$`) before it is ever concatenated into a response body served with an executable content type; if validation fails, reject the request (e.g. HTTP 400) rather than silently stripping/truncating (silent truncation can itself be bypassed). Because IoUtil.streamResponseAndClose is shared, the cleanest fix centralizes validation there (or in a shared helper called by all four sink sites) rather than only in one caller \u2014 otherwise the sibling path stays exploitable. Concretely the fix must cover, and regression tests should re-check, all four sites:\n  - IoUtil.streamResponseAndClose (agent/core/src/main/java/org/jolokia/util/IoUtil.java:36)\n  - AgentServlet.sendAllJSON (agent/core/src/main/java/org/jolokia/http/AgentServlet.java:500)\n  - JolokiaHttpHandler.sendStreamingResponse \u2192 IoUtil (agent/jvm/src/main/java/org/jolokia/jvmagent/handler/JolokiaHttpHandler.java:348)\n  - JolokiaHttpHandler.sendAllJSON (agent/jvm/src/main/java/org/jolokia/jvmagent/handler/JolokiaHttpHandler.java:364)\n\nKnown bypass variants the fix must also block, since the callback source differs by agent flavor and by how the parameter is decoded:\n  - Servlet flavor: `callback` obtained via `HttpServletRequest.getParameter()` for both GET query string and POST bodies \u2014 validate regardless of HTTP method.\n  - JVM-agent flavor: `callback` obtained via ParsedUri's own hand-rolled URL-decoding (ParsedUri.java:131 `URLDecoder.decode(...)`) \u2014 a fix must validate the *decoded* value (not just the raw query bytes), and must cover both the single-value assignment branch (ParsedUri.java:135) and the multi-value/list branch (ParsedUri.java:143), since JolokiaHttpHandler.java:345/362 both read back through `ParsedUri.getParameter()` regardless of which branch populated it.\n  - Non-identifier payloads that terminate the callback early and inject trailing statements (e.g. `foo//`, `foo;bar`, `foo</script><script>...`, whitespace/newline-containing values, or values using `\\u` escapes) should all be rejected by the same whitelist regex rather than only blacklisting specific characters like `(` or `<`.\n  - Content-Type coupling: confirm the fix does not merely change the default MIME type while still writing the raw callback \u2014 the byte-level response content itself must be validated/rejected, not just relabeled.",
